{"id":"H4322","lemma":"מִיכָיָ֫הוּ","transliteration":"mikhayahu","sayIt":"mi-kha-YA-hu","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Micaiah","meaning":"A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.17.7\n§ Michaiah = \"who is like God\"\n1) one of the princes of Jehoshaphat whom he sent to teach the law of Jehovah in the cities of Judah\n2) daughter of Uriel of Gibeah, wife of king Rehoboam of Judah, and mother of king Abijah of Judah","glosses":["micaiah"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"2ch-13","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"was Micaiah","kjv":"also was Michaiah"}},{"chapterId":"2ch-17","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"and Micaiah","kjv":"and to Michaiah"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"2 Chronicles 13:2","note":"He reigned three years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Micaiah the daughter of Uriel of Gibeah. There was war between Abijah and Jeroboam.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H0222","lemma":"אוּרִיאֵל","transliteration":"uriel","gloss":"Uriel"},{"id":"H8559","lemma":"תָּמָר","transliteration":"tamar","gloss":"Tamar"},{"id":"H7346","lemma":"רְחַבְעָם","transliteration":"rechavam","gloss":"Rehoboam"},{"id":"H0029","lemma":"אֲבִיָּה","transliteration":"aviyyah","gloss":"Abijah"},{"id":"H6262","lemma":"עַתַּי","transliteration":"attay","gloss":"Attai"},{"id":"H2124","lemma":"זִיזָא","transliteration":"ziza","gloss":"Ziza"},{"id":"H8019","lemma":"שְׁלֹמִית","transliteration":"shelomit","gloss":"Shelomith"},{"id":"H4601","lemma":"מַעֲכָה","transliteration":"maakhah","gloss":"Maacah"}],"senses":[{"id":"H4322H","gloss":"Micaiah","relation":"H4322H = a Name of"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}